  "notes": "Two 2923 nm beams (HeNe tracers) combined on knife edge KE1, 57 um apart on the sample.\n1 Co-align one arm at a time on the alignment board below this one: seat its pick-off (M9 top / M8 bottom, K);\n  both send their sample straight down off the bottom edge at x = 7.5\".\n  HeNe: walk M7+BS2 (M6+BS1). 2923: walk M4+M3 (M5+M2). Lift the pick-off.\n2 Per arm, M20 (M21) does the walking: tilt it to place that arm's spot (10 um per mrad);\n  slide it along its incoming beam to move that arm on KE1 and in the pupil (1:1, the spot stays).\n3 M22+M23 walk both beams onto the objective together.\n4 Slide KE1 along the beams to make them cross in the pupil: 1 mm per mm, the spots do not move.\nSee docs/alignment.md.",
